# Open Source Credits must be complete (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-18): **You must include ALL open source
licenses in our disclosure.** Not a curated subset.

Operator clarification (Phil, 2026-08-18): **Open Source Credits do not need
to be localized. They do need to be complete and always up to date.**

## The rule

> **Every shipping OSS disclosure (`/about/open-source-credits`,
> `GET /api/admin/open-source-credits`, and the embedded inventory) must
> list every third-party open-source component incorporated into AIC
> Server: the full Cargo production graph (registry + git), the full npm
> production graph, and incorporated assets (for example lipis/flag-icons).
> Each entry must carry a license SPDX/name and the actual license text
> (harvested or a stored copy of the licensor's published text). Status
> may be Live only when every package has identity + text. Packages that
> truly lack a harvestable license stay listed as BLOCKED — never silently
> omitted, never invented. The inventory is US English only (licensor
> language / English disclosure). Do not localize the credits page,
> inventory, license bodies, or copyright notices. Regenerate from current
> lockfiles on every server deploy and MSI/package path so a lockfile
> change cannot ship a stale list.**

## Required

1. Regenerate with `core-assets/scripts/generate-open-source-credits.py`
   against current `pim-offline-server/Cargo.lock` and
   `ui/package-lock.json` (run `cargo fetch --locked` first when registry
   crates are missing locally). Inputs also include incorporated assets
   (flag-icons, etc.).
2. Harvest bodies from the Cargo registry / git checkouts, `node_modules`,
   and in-tree LICENSE files — do not hand-type license text from memory.
3. **Always-current seam:** invoke regeneration (fail-closed on BLOCKED)
   from `Deploy-OfflineServerDev.ps1` and the AIC Server MSI/package
   path via `Invoke-OpenSourceCreditsRegen.ps1`. `pim-offline-server/build.rs`
   refuses a stale inventory (lockfile SHA mismatch) so `cargo build`
   cannot embed an old list. Do **not** add push-triggered CI
   ([`ci-policy.mdc`](ci-policy.mdc)).
4. Fail closed: `--require-live` / regen exit non-zero when any third-party
   package lacks license identity or text. First-party path crates may stay
   excluded when already documented in the generator.
5. Honesty banner: inventory status + generation SHAs (Cargo.lock,
   package-lock, companion SBOM when present) so an operator can confirm
   the list matches this build.
6. Page: searchable list; expandable license text; honesty banner;
   pagination or virtualization is OK for large graphs. SPA locale may be
   German (or any pack) while the credits page remains English — intentional.
7. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change set.

## Forbidden

- Curated-direct-only inventories, or "Partial because we only list directs"
- Omitting transitive Cargo or npm production packages
- Inventing SPDX ids or license bodies
- Dropping packages that lack a license file instead of marking **BLOCKED**
- Shipping a committed inventory whose lockfile SHAs do not match the
  current `Cargo.lock` / `package-lock.json`
- Silent deploy/package success when status is not Live (BLOCKED present)
- Localizing credits chrome / inventory / license bodies, or enqueueing
  must-localize work for this page
- Claiming Met / certified for the disclosure

